cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ABMfact, please cite it as below."
title: "ABMfact: run agent-based models across simulators and check their conclusions"
abstract: >-
  ABMfact runs agent-based models in several simulators through one interface and checks whether their
  conclusions are findings or implementation artefacts. Models run in their own format or are written in
  ABM-IR, a shared description translated for each simulator with a report of what was kept exactly,
  approximated or dropped. Every run is recorded with its engine version, settings and seed. ABMfact
  reruns a model under changes that a correct implementation must not care about, such as activation
  order, agent labels, random streams, grid placement, time step, voxel size and population size, and
  reports which stated conclusions survive, with intervals and reproducible commands.
type: software
